{
  "$comment": [
    "Copy to .mcp.json (which is gitignored — it is local client state, not source).",
    "",
    "Why this file exists: .mcp.json and .vscode/mcp.json previously registered the",
    "SecB MCP server as `npx -y secb-agent-registry@latest`. That package name is",
    "unpublished, and npx resolves against the public registry here (no .npmrc, no",
    "private mirror), so the name was claimable by anyone — after which `-y` would",
    "fetch and execute it without a prompt. Both files are gitignored, so the",
    "corrected form lived on one machine and nowhere in the repository; the next",
    "person wiring up MCP had nothing to copy and the npx form was what they would",
    "have found. This file is the corrected form, in the repository, on purpose.",
    "",
    "The command below routes through the local dispatcher instead, which removes",
    "the resolution path entirely. `secb mcp serve` still refuses to start without",
    "SECB_MCP_DEPLOYMENT_AUTHORIZED=operator: that gate lives in",
    "tools/run-secb-mcp-server.mjs and the dispatcher does not reach past it, so",
    "registering the server is not the same as activating it (working rule 5).",
    "",
    "The args path is relative and resolves against the client's working directory.",
    "Clients that launch servers from the project root need no change; anywhere",
    "else, make it absolute. Only the entry point is affected — tools/secb.mjs",
    "resolves its own targets against the repository root, so subcommands behave",
    "identically from any directory."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "secb": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": [
        "tools/secb.mjs",
        "mcp",
        "serve"
      ]
    }
  }
}
